      {
        "id": 262818,
        "name": "KateWalker",
        "username": "TakeWalker",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
        "created_at": "2025-03-11T19:16:40.643Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This cover rocks. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=12\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>I need to be nicer to my knees, I <em>still</em> have a huge bruise on one that I don’t remember getting. c_c;</p>\n<p>Oh, they’ve never talked about this foe on the air before? So Calypso is actually Busybody?\\ then.</p>\n<p>lmao, Indiana Jones was inspired by Ra? XD</p>\n<p>Who knew Calypso and Wipeout were the same person all this time?</p>\n<p>Oh, she plays Calypso in a movie? Okay, this character is way more fun than I could have imagined, I like this a lot.</p>\n<p>Collapso is a really good name for a Silver Age villain with a dumb gimmick. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>“I’m Calypso! I sing to your spirit! The men who have served me so long and so well!”</p>\n<p><em>Can</em> Ra run out of fire? <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/thinking.png?v=12\" title=\":thinking:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":thinking:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>She’s the only villain who wants to be a-Nile-ated. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=12\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> She’s clearly in de-Nile!</p>\n<p>Wow, so you can drink Calypso, but you can’t drink Guise? Double-standard much???</p>\n<p>Don’t come between a sun god and his cupcakes. 8| Cupcakes are serious business.</p>\n<p>It wasn’t really Segaeiuodoth, it was Old Man Apostate in a rubber mask! Again!</p>\n<p>And then when the Aeon Bears get their mitts on Aeon Berry Juice, all bets are off.</p>\n<p>I feel like WolfTek <em>should</em> be the answer to Oblivaeon…</p>\n<p>Gumbo becomes a hero, confirmed. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=12\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>Justice for Schleep-Schlorp! LMAO, Christopher literally said it as I was typing this! XD</p>\n<p>It me! <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=12\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>They joke, but I would legitimately enjoy catching those references in Sentinels. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>Painstake’s mom as a scion is a great concept, damn. And an equally good reason not to have her to do it, that’s pretty unusual.</p>",
