        "raw": "This cover rocks. :D\n\nI need to be nicer to my knees, I *still* have a huge bruise on one that I don't remember getting. c_c;\n\nOh, they've never talked about this foe on the air before? So Calypso is actually Busybody?\\ then.\n\nlmao, Indiana Jones was inspired by Ra? XD\n\nWho knew Calypso and Wipeout were the same person all this time?\n\nOh, she plays Calypso in a movie? Okay, this character is way more fun than I could have imagined, I like this a lot.\n\nCollapso is a really good name for a Silver Age villain with a dumb gimmick. :)\n\n\"I'm Calypso! I sing to your spirit! The men who have served me so long and so well!\"\n\n*Can* Ra run out of fire? :thinking:\n\nShe's the only villain who wants to be a-Nile-ated. :D She's clearly in de-Nile!\n\nWow, so you can drink Calypso, but you can't drink Guise? Double-standard much???\n\nDon't come between a sun god and his cupcakes. 8| Cupcakes are serious business.\n\nIt wasn't really Segaeiuodoth, it was Old Man Apostate in a rubber mask! Again!\n\nAnd then when the Aeon Bears get their mitts on Aeon Berry Juice, all bets are off.\n\nI feel like WolfTek *should* be the answer to Oblivaeon...\n\nGumbo becomes a hero, confirmed. :D\n\nJustice for Schleep-Schlorp! LMAO, Christopher literally said it as I was typing this! XD\n\nIt me! :D\n\nThey joke, but I would legitimately enjoy catching those references in Sentinels. :)\n\nPainstake's mom as a scion is a great concept, damn. And an equally good reason not to have her to do it, that's pretty unusual.",
